<Item XName="EqnBlock" Type="EqnBlock">
<Lang><T>Int</T><D>1</D></Lang></Item>
<Item XName="Font" Type="Font">
<Name>Courier New</Name>
<Size><T>Double</T><D>125</D></Size></Item>
<Item XName="FunctionBlock" Type="FunctionBlock" />
<Item XName="VarBlock" Type="VarBlock" /></Item>
<Item XName="Note" UserName="Note" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;FONT color=#0000ff size=6&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in; BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; PADDING-TOP: 0in&quot; class=MsoTitle align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=5 face=Arial&gt;MSR Base Station Out Of Band Blocking&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal align=center&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: Arial; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Example Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = o ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoBodyText&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2&gt;This example demonstrates how to measure the MSR base station out of band blocking according to clause&amp;nbsp;7.5 of 3GPP TS 37.141.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 9pt&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&gt;The Out-of-band blocking characteristic is a measure of the receiver ability to receive a wanted signal at its assigned channel in the presence of an unwanted interferer outside the uplink operating band. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;FONT face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&gt;The test stresses the ability of the BS receiver to withstand high-level interference from unwanted signals at specified frequency bands, without undue degradation of its sensitivity.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2 face=Arial&gt;In this example, one LTE&amp;nbsp;carrier and one WCDMA carrier from MSR Band&amp;nbsp;11 (1427.9MHz - 1447.9MHz) and one LTE carrier and one WCDMA carrier from MSR Band 10( 1710MHz - 1770MHz) are combined using SingalCombiner part. The interfering signal is a CW signal. The MSR bands definition can be found in Table 4.4-1 of 3GPP TS 37.104.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2 face=Arial&gt;Equation &lt;EM&gt;TestConfiguration&lt;/EM&gt; specifies the used MSR Band and the signal configurations of each carrier e.g. sampling rate and bandwidth.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2&gt;The spectrum graph &quot;MSR_spec_Power&quot; shows the combined spectrum, while the spectrum graph &quot;MSR_spec_Power with individual spectrums&quot; shows the combined spectrum along with individual standard spectrum.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2&gt;Table &quot;TestResults&quot; shows the measured bit error rate of WCDMA carrier and throughput fraction of LTE carrier.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;TRY THIS:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;OL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2 face=Arial&gt;Change MSR bands in equation &lt;EM&gt;TestConfiguration&lt;/EM&gt; by setting F_F_Block1_BWlow, F_F_Block1_BWhigh, F_Block2_BWlow, F_Block2_BWlhigh and F_BWmid.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000&gt;Change the interferer configuraiton in equation T&lt;EM&gt;estConfiguration.&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000&gt;Change the wanted signal configuration in equation &lt;EM&gt;TestConfiguration.&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 face=Arial&gt;Sweep the interfere frequency offset using Sweep1.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 face=Arial&gt;Adjust the noise density in &lt;EM&gt;AddNdensity &lt;/EM&gt;model in the design.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/OL&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;</Text>
